# protobuf's Python JSON parser expanded nested google.protobuf.Any
# messages through a reflective method dispatch that skipped the
# recursion-depth accounting, so deeply nested Any input bypassed
# max_recursion_depth and overflowed the stack (denial of service
# through a budget-bypassing branch, CWE-400/CWE-1327; #25239, fixed
# with #25587). _Parser.ConvertMessage in
# python/google/protobuf/json_format.py is the budget-checked entry:
# recursion_depth += 1, the max_recursion_depth comparison, and the
# decrement on exit. Its well-known-type branch dispatches through
# methodcaller(_WKTJSONMETHODS[full_name][1], ...)(self) -- accounted
# for, because the increment already ran. _ConvertAnyMessage, reached
# through that same table for google.protobuf.Any, had a second
# methodcaller branch of its own that re-entered the parser without
# passing ConvertMessage, so nested Any never paid the increment.
# Pool commit 5ebddcb1bc is the real fix ("Fix Any recursion depth
# bypass in Python json_format.ParseDict"): the _ConvertAnyMessage
# branch calls self.ConvertMessage(value['value'], sub_message,
# '{0}.value'.format(path)) so every nested message -- Any included --
# is counted, with a regression test nesting five Anys under
# max_recursion_depth=5. The budget-covered methodcaller branch in
# ConvertMessage stays as it was. No pool correction.
#
# Held ATTENTION, budget-bypassing dispatch, rechecked at the span tip.
# Fresh 3 x --cache off scans of the real checkout: json_format.py
# alone reports 0 findings at both revisions (6 core.PathAccessCheck
# flags on `in` operators and a core.SafeDeserialization control, the
# only labels in either view), and the whole python/google/protobuf
# tree reports 98 findings at both revisions with none on
# json_format.py, so the 1st-pass zero is genuine in the full findings
# view, not a -flags misread. Nothing in the recursion family fires:
# VYQL-DOS-029's concept has a C binding only, VYQL-DOS-016 is the
# bespoke Gson classifier, VYQL-DOS-035/045 have no Python emitters,
# and VYQL-DOS-042's Python emitters key on asyncio task registries
# and streaming decompressors. The label surface exists -- vyql graph
# emits code.Call path=operator.methodcaller at the bypassing site --
# but no verdict is reachable from it: the dispatch target is
# _WKTJSONMETHODS[full_name][1], a dict lookup keyed by a runtime
# descriptor string, with no resolvable edge into any _Convert*
# method, and re-entry unification is a recorded engine limit
# (1320/1391/1697). The discriminating fact is measured to be the
# method, not the construct: the identical reflective dispatch appears
# at two sites in the budget-bearing class -- ConvertMessage's
# budget-covered branch and _ConvertAnyMessage's bypassing branch --
# and the fix removes only the second while the first survives, so a
# class-scope "budget-bearing class using reflective dispatch" binding
# fires at both revisions and a method-scope binding flags the safe
# site at both; the only clean 1 -> 0 discriminator is keying on the
# method that must route through ConvertMessage, the fixing commit's
# own layout. A binding on _WKTJSONMETHODS or _ConvertAnyMessage
# detects this library rather than the weakness: the table and the
# method names are undocumented internals. methodcaller is absent from
# the Python benchmark corpus, so a bare reflective-dispatch label
# would be benchmark-neutral and verdict-free -- the missing thing is
# the dispatch-path completeness question, not the label. Second
# vehicle of the 1262 counter-bypass family (reflective dispatch
# instead of a fresh instance); no standalone ENGINE-GAPS.md entry,
# restated there instead. No definition change shipped. This spec pins
# both revisions on the real class shape -- both methodcaller sites
# present in the vulnerable form, the fix swapping only
# _ConvertAnyMessage's branch to ConvertMessage -- rejecting
# VYQL-DOS-029 and VYQL-DOS-042: when depth-budget vocabulary lands,
# the bypassing form must flip to expect on whichever fires.

test "rank1612: the well-known branch bypasses the depth budget"
  lang python
  file python/google/protobuf/json_format.py
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  code
  ```
  from operator import methodcaller


  _WKTJSONMETHODS = {
      'google.protobuf.Any': ('', '_ConvertAnyMessage'),
      'google.protobuf.Duration': ('', '_ConvertDurationMessage'),
  }


  class _Parser(object):

    def __init__(self, ignore_unknown_fields, descriptor_pool,
                 max_recursion_depth):
      self.ignore_unknown_fields = ignore_unknown_fields
      self.descriptor_pool = descriptor_pool
      self.max_recursion_depth = max_recursion_depth
      self.recursion_depth = 0

    def ConvertMessage(self, value, message, path):
      self.recursion_depth += 1
      if self.recursion_depth > self.max_recursion_depth:
        raise ParseError('Message too deep.')
      message_descriptor = message.DESCRIPTOR
      full_name = message_descriptor.full_name
      if _IsWrapperMessage(message_descriptor):
        self._ConvertWrapperMessage(value, message, path)
      elif full_name in _WKTJSONMETHODS:
        methodcaller(
            _WKTJSONMETHODS[full_name][1], value, message, path
        )(self)
      else:
        self._ConvertFieldValuePair(value, message, path)
      self.recursion_depth -= 1

    def _ConvertAnyMessage(self, value, message, path):
      type_url = value['@type']
      sub_message = _CreateMessageFromTypeUrl(
          type_url, self.descriptor_pool
      )
      full_name = sub_message.DESCRIPTOR.full_name
      if _IsWrapperMessage(sub_message.DESCRIPTOR):
        self._ConvertWrapperMessage(
            value['value'], sub_message, '{0}.value'.format(path)
        )
      elif full_name in _WKTJSONMETHODS:
        methodcaller(
            _WKTJSONMETHODS[full_name][1],
            value['value'],
            sub_message,
            '{0}.value'.format(path),
        )(self)
      else:
        self._ConvertFieldValuePair(value, sub_message, path)
      message.value = sub_message.SerializeToString()
      message.type_url = type_url
  ```

test "rank1612: the fixed revision routes the branch through the budget"
  lang python
  file python/google/protobuf/json_format.py
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  code
  ```
  from operator import methodcaller


  _WKTJSONMETHODS = {
      'google.protobuf.Any': ('', '_ConvertAnyMessage'),
      'google.protobuf.Duration': ('', '_ConvertDurationMessage'),
  }


  class _Parser(object):

    def __init__(self, ignore_unknown_fields, descriptor_pool,
                 max_recursion_depth):
      self.ignore_unknown_fields = ignore_unknown_fields
      self.descriptor_pool = descriptor_pool
      self.max_recursion_depth = max_recursion_depth
      self.recursion_depth = 0

    def ConvertMessage(self, value, message, path):
      self.recursion_depth += 1
      if self.recursion_depth > self.max_recursion_depth:
        raise ParseError('Message too deep.')
      message_descriptor = message.DESCRIPTOR
      full_name = message_descriptor.full_name
      if _IsWrapperMessage(message_descriptor):
        self._ConvertWrapperMessage(value, message, path)
      elif full_name in _WKTJSONMETHODS:
        methodcaller(
            _WKTJSONMETHODS[full_name][1], value, message, path
        )(self)
      else:
        self._ConvertFieldValuePair(value, message, path)
      self.recursion_depth -= 1

    def _ConvertAnyMessage(self, value, message, path):
      type_url = value['@type']
      sub_message = _CreateMessageFromTypeUrl(
          type_url, self.descriptor_pool
      )
      full_name = sub_message.DESCRIPTOR.full_name
      if _IsWrapperMessage(sub_message.DESCRIPTOR):
        self._ConvertWrapperMessage(
            value['value'], sub_message, '{0}.value'.format(path)
        )
      elif full_name in _WKTJSONMETHODS:
        # For well-known types (including nested Any), use ConvertMessage
        # to ensure recursion depth is properly tracked
        self.ConvertMessage(
            value['value'], sub_message, '{0}.value'.format(path)
        )
      else:
        self._ConvertFieldValuePair(value, sub_message, path)
      message.value = sub_message.SerializeToString()
      message.type_url = type_url
